  "id": "Compound::DB00884 - Gene::2224",
  "verbalization": "Risedronate, a diphosphonate, is implicated in the interaction with Fdps through multiple mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Risedronate, as part of the diphosphonate class, binds to Fdps, with a shared lowest common ancestor of Pnictogen Molecular Entity, indicating a common structural or functional category. This binding is corroborated by the presence of similar interactions in both Risedronate and Ibandronate, which also bind to Fdps, further supporting a general mechanism of phosphonic acid-mediated interaction with Fdps. The evidence also highlights that Risedronate can cause an increase in Blood Parathyroid Hormone, which is subsequently caused by Ibandronate, suggesting a potential chain of effects involving Fdps. The integration of these pathways underscores a consistent mechanism of action involving phosphonic acid binding to Fdps, with Risedronate and Ibandronate both contributing to this interaction. The observed scores and shared ancestry suggest a robust, mechanistically sound relationship between Risedronate and Fdps, supported by multiple independent pathways.",
